{"content":[{"c":["MAACAH, MAACHAH* (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common Hebrew name, often spelled Maachah in the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Last of the four children of Nahor, Abraham’s brother, by Reumah his concubine (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.22.24","r":"Gen.22.24","rawR":"Gen.22.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.22.24","value":"Gen.22.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 22:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-space","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Daughter of Talmai, king of Geshur, a wife of David, and Absalom’s mother (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.3.3","r":"2Sam.3.3","rawR":"2Sam.3.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.3.3","value":"2Sam.3.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 3:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.2","r":"1Chr.3.2","rawR":"1Chr.3.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.2","value":"1Chr.3.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Achish’s father. Achish, king of Gath, housed two of Shimei’s slaves during Solomon’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.2.39","r":"1Kgs.2.39","rawR":"1Kgs.2.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.2.39","value":"1Kgs.2.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 2:39"},"). He is identified with Maoch in ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.27.2","r":"1Sam.27.2","rawR":"1Sam.27.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.27.2","value":"1Sam.27.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Samuel 27:2"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Maoch_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Maoch_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Maoch_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Maoch"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Daughter of Absalom (Abishalom) (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.2,10","r":"1Kgs.15.2,10","rawR":"1Kgs.15.2,10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.2,10","value":"1Kgs.15.2,10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 15:2, 10"},"), the wife of Rehoboam, king of Judah (930–913 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), and the mother of King Abijah (913–910 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") and grandmother of King Asa (910–869 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.10","r":"1Kgs.15.10","rawR":"1Kgs.15.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.10","value":"1Kgs.15.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 15:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.20-22","r":"2Chr.11.20-22","rawR":"2Chr.11.20-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.20-22","value":"2Chr.11.20-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:20-22"},"). Later, Asa removed her as queen mother because she had an idol made for Asherah (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.10-13","r":"1Kgs.15.10-13","rawR":"1Kgs.15.10-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.10-13","value":"1Kgs.15.10-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 15:10-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.15.16","r":"2Chr.15.16","rawR":"2Chr.15.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.15.16","value":"2Chr.15.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 15:16"},"). Maacah is spelled Micaiah (Michaiah) in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.2","r":"2Chr.13.2","rawR":"2Chr.13.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.2","value":"2Chr.13.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 13:2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Caleb’s concubine and the mother of four sons (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.48","r":"1Chr.2.48","rawR":"1Chr.2.48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.48","value":"1Chr.2.48"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:48"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Sister of Huppim and Shuppim, the wife of Makir the Manassite and mother of Peresh and Sheresh (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.15-16","r":"1Chr.7.15-16","rawR":"1Chr.7.15-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.15-16","value":"1Chr.7.15-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:15-16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Benjamite, the wife of Jeiel, and an ancestress of King Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.29","r":"1Chr.8.29","rawR":"1Chr.8.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.29","value":"1Chr.8.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.35","r":"1Chr.9.35","rawR":"1Chr.9.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.35","value":"1Chr.9.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Father of Haman, one of David’s mighty warriors (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.43","r":"1Chr.11.43","rawR":"1Chr.11.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.43","value":"1Chr.11.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:43"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["9. Father of Shephatiah, chief officer of Simeon’s tribe during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.16","r":"1Chr.27.16","rawR":"1Chr.27.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.16","value":"1Chr.27.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MaacahMaachahPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 22:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.22.24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.22.24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.22.24"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 3:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.3.3","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.3.3","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.3.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 2:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.2.39","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.2.39","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.2.39"},{"anchorText":"1 Samuel 27:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.27.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.27.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.27.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 15:2, 10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.15.2,10","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.15.2,10","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.15.2,10"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 15:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.15.10","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.15.10","sourceRefExact